+# U-Net style encoder->decoder skip connections (modded-nanogpt records 8+). The outputs of the
+# first n_enc = depth // 2 blocks are added, LIFO, into the residual entering the last n_enc
+# blocks through one learnable per-channel FP32 vector each (GPT.unet_skip_gates). Every vector
+# is ZERO-initialised (nn.Parameter(torch.zeros) draws no torch RNG), so at step 0 the forward
+# graph is bit-identical to the control: x + 0 * h == x for finite x. Distinct from the x0 gate
+# (reads the embedding, not block outputs), the frozen block nudge and the final-output pooling.
+# The vectors ride the gate/conv AdamW group in setup_optimizer (MATRIX_LR, betas (0.9, 0.95),
+# wd 0.0), never Muon and never the SCALAR_LR group. CLI: --unet-skip / --no-unet-skip.
+USE_UNET_SKIP = os.environ.get("NEURON_COMPETITION_R1_UNET_SKIP", "1") != "0"
